Module parity.syntax.keywordcasepositions.

Define Color as one of Red Or Green, Blue AND Black oR White and Gray.
Define Shade as one of Light OR Dark.

Define Point with x as Int
And y as Int
AND z as Int.

Define Pair has left as Int, right as Int.

Rule add given a as Int And b as Int AND c as Int, produce Int:
  Return a plus b plus c.

Rule inc given v as Int, produce Int:
  Return v plus 1.

Rule bump given n as Int, produce Int:
  Let m be apply inc To n.
  Return apply inc TO m.

Rule origin, produce Point:
  Return Point with x set to 0 and y SET to 0 AND z Set to 0.

Rule pair given n as Int, produce Pair:
  Return Pair has left set to n and right sET to 0.

Rule other given n as Int, produce Pair:
  Return Pair HAS left set to n, right set to n.

Rule third given n as Int, produce Pair:
  Let p be Pair Has left set to 1 and right set to n.
  Return p.

Rule sum given v as Int, produce Int:
  Let f be function given a as Int And b as Int, produce Int: Return a plus b.
  Let g be function with a as Int AND b as Int aND c as Int, produce Int: Return a plus b plus c.
  Return f(v, g(v, v, v)).
